cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite the paper below."
title: "Benign-Only Ransomware Detection via Dual-Channel Behavioral Anomaly Fusion: A Feasibility Study"
abstract: >-
  Code for a feasibility study of benign-only, dual-channel ransomware
  anomaly detection. Two Gaussian Mixture Models trained on benign data
  only (sandbox API/static-artifact features and hypervisor block-I/O
  metrics) are fused by a learned density model over bootstrap-paired
  benign scores. Fusion is not an accuracy gain on the saturated
  benchmark; under attack it degrades gracefully when one channel is
  compromised and fails when both are (AUC 0.326).
